for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nD:\\HMS Project\\HMS1\\src\\features\\appointments\\components\\AppointmentDatePickerFilter.tsx:47:9\n  45 |       const d = new Date(selectedDate);\n  46 |       if (!isNaN(d.getTime())) {\n> 47 |         setViewYear(d.getFullYear());\n     |         ^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  48 |         setViewMonth(d.getMonth());\n  49 |       }\n  50 |     }","react-hooks/exhaustive-deps","React Hook useMemo has an unnecessary dependency: 'todayDateStr'. Either exclude it or remove the dependency array.",["3024"],{"desc":"3025","fix":"3026"},"Update the dependencies array to be: [roleAppointments, filters, dateFilter, sortColumn, sortDirection]",{"range":"3027","text":"3028"},[9936,10052],"[roleAppointments, filters, dateFilter, sortColumn, sortDirection]"]